{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"piscine-bullish-cowbird","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAt audited code snapshot `9a94ef9737fbdf070ae314bba6e797319aee2301`,\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py:1-800` and\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile_helpers.py:1-800` are exactly at the locked\n800-line module-size cap. Any net addition fails the existing CI gate. Brant's existing\n`wormlike-buried-grunion` prerequisite restores headroom in `run_differs.py`,\n`outbound_differ.py`, and `applier.py`; it deliberately does not own these two spine modules.\n\nThe prior RP-03 work made `reconcile_once` a thin lifecycle sequencer over existing load, diff,\napply, and persist phases and introduced the current per-pass state carrier. Preserve that decision.\nThe pre-observation repair boundary from ADR 0099 is load-bearing: repair remains after the\nunder-lock staleness check and before the first remote fetch.\n\nProvenance: janitor finding S14 (validity 0.90, impact 1.00), discovered during\n`literal-subaverage-dartfrog`. This story restores optionality needed by Brant; it does not add\ntyped-payload behavior.\n\n## Approach / End State\n\n- Re-measure both modules against the current Brant prerequisite tip before editing and record the\n  baseline.\n- Restore real headroom through deletion or extraction of cohesive phase-owned call-graph clusters.\n  Current candidate seams are `_load_snapshots`, `_apply_mutations`, `_persist_and_log`, and\n  their existing helper families; use the contract story's final ownership decision if it changes\n  those seams.\n- Keep `reconcile_once` as the lifecycle facade and reuse the existing pass state. Do not introduce\n  a second generic pass/ticket context or move unrelated behavior merely to reduce a number.\n- Preserve public/import/monkeypatch compatibility only where the census proves a supported\n  consumer. Re-anchor structural tests when a symbol legitimately moves rather than retaining a\n  compatibility cycle.\n- Preserve the ADR 0099 repair ordering with a behavioral oracle that is proven to fail when repair\n  moves after observation.\n\n`cascade_flag=true`: these modules are high-centrality orchestration surfaces. Census semantic\ncallers plus string/dynamic references, including monkeypatch, `getattr`, importlib, file-path\nloading, complexity-baseline keys, and structural tests.\n\n## Sequencing\n\nThis story follows `scummy-ultrashort-tuatara` so the accepted payload/producer contract fixes the\nownership boundary, runs in parallel with the disjoint `wormlike-buried-grunion` extraction, and\nmust close before `earthborn-statuelike-boutu` adds typed-payload implementation.\n\n## Testing\n\nUse the existing reconciler orchestration and recovery-boundary suites unchanged except for\nnecessary import/structural re-anchors. Run the module-size and complexity gates, lint, typecheck,\nand the focused reconciler suite. Seed a post-fetch repair move and observe the ordering test fail\nbefore restoring the correct order.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The pre-change baseline is recorded against the current prerequisite tip; if either cited\n      module was already brought below 700 lines, no replacement work is invented for that module.\n- [ ] `reconcile.py` and `reconcile_helpers.py` are each at or below 700 lines on the completed\n      tree, without changing the locked 800-line limit.\n- [ ] Every new module is at least 100 lines and represents a cohesive existing call-graph cluster;\n      no split is mechanical and resulting modules follow the 200-500 LOC target where practicable.\n- [ ] `reconcile_once` remains the single lifecycle facade and no second generic pass/ticket\n      context or duplicate operation authority is introduced.\n- [ ] Repair remains after `ensure_selection_current` and before the first remote fetch; the\n      behavioral oracle is demonstrated RED under a seeded post-fetch move and GREEN after restore.\n- [ ] Semantic references and a repository string/dynamic-reference sweep are recorded for every\n      moved symbol, and supported monkeypatch/import surfaces continue to resolve without a cycle.\n- [ ] Existing reconciler behavior is unchanged: focused orchestration/recovery suites pass without\n      weakened assertions, and Brant's portable parity corpus remains green once available.\n- [ ] Module-size, complexity-ratchet, lint, and typecheck gates pass with no limit or baseline\n      increase.","id":"0f21-a181-be4f-4fe8","parent_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915","priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["architecture","reconciler","maintainability","module-size","janitor"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Restore reconciler spine headroom before typed-payload implementation"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788055318800917611,"uuid":"00deda96-ba0f-42e7-a94f-039774bcae3a"}